---
title: Clay Pot Chicken Rice
servings: 4
course: dinner
cuisine: Chinese
tags: chicken, rice, one-pan, quick
source: https://www.food.com/recipe/76012
prep time: 10m
cook time: 25m
---

-- the source cooks this in a clay pot over a medium flame; the rice cooker does the same job
-- unattended, which is the point of it

Chop @chicken thigh{250%g} and marinate it in @light soy sauce{1%tbsp} while you measure the rest.

Put @long grain rice{300%g}, @chicken stock{500%ml}, @garlic{1%tbsp}(minced) and @shallot{1%tbsp}(minced) into the #rice cooker{}. Stir in @dark soy sauce{1%tbsp}, @oyster sauce{1%tbsp}, @white pepper{1%tsp} and @sesame oil{1%tsp}.

Close the lid and start it. Leave it shut until the stock is nearly absorbed, about ~{15%minutes}.

Open the lid and tip in the marinated chicken and @?chinese sausage{1}(sliced). Close the lid again and cook for another ~{10-15%minutes}.

Stir the rice so it does not stick to the bottom, and cook until it is soft and fluffy. Serve, with more @&dark soy sauce{} and @&white pepper{} to taste.
